rate AI growth - Gulfdays. (https://gulfdays.net/saudi-arabia-to-develop-over-14-gw-of-computing-capacity-to-accelerate-ai-growth/)\nciteturn11search3 [wordlim: 200] Published: 2 days ago; Crawled: today; SILICON VALLEY — Saudi Arabia is working with the private sector to develop more than 14 gigawatts of computing capacity as it builds an integrated model to attract artificial intelligence companies and accelerate their growth, Minister of Communications and Information Technology Abdullah Al-Swaha said.Speaking at the opening of the fourth Frontier Leaders Forum 2026 in Silicon Valley, California, Al-Swaha said the Kingdom’s approach centers on providing AI companies with three critical components: computing capacity, capital and access to customers.The forum, held under the theme “AI Forward: A Global Frontier,” brought together leaders from AI, technology, investment, venture capital and innovation from the United States and around the world.Al-Swaha cited Groq as an example of the model, saying Saudi Arabia was among the company’s early supporters by providing access to major customers, investing in the company and creating an environment that enabled it to scale.He said the Kingdom aims to replicate that experience with a new generation of global companies.Al-Swaha said the more than 14 GW of computing capacity being developed in partnership with the private sector would support the requirements of advanced AI companies, reduce operating costs and improve infrastructure efficiency.He also highlighted Saudi Arabia’s expanding adoption of generative, agentic and physical AI, ranging from healthcare applications and AI agents supporting government employees to autonomous systems in transportation and logistics.The Kingdom will continue strengthening its partnership with Silicon Valley through talent, technology and trust, while providing computing capacity, customers and capital to enable the next generation of AI companies to grow and scale globally, he said.During his visit, Al-Swaha held a series of meetings focused on expanding AI investment, developing advanced models and applications, and integrating them with infrastructure and computing capacity being developed by HUMAIN.He met General Catalyst CEO Hemant Taneja to discuss expanding the company’s investments in AI and advanced technologies in Saudi Arabia and enabling its portfolio companies to develop and deploy applied AI solutions using HUMAIN’s computing capacity in priority sectors.Al-Swaha also met Arcee AI founder and CEO Mark McQuade to discuss expanding the use of the company’s open Trinity models and customized enterprise models through HUMAIN’s infrastructure.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nBoudl Al Munsiyah: 2026 Deals & Reviews | Trip.com (https://uk.trip.com/hotels/riyadh-hotel-detail-15009317/boudl-al-munsiyah/)\nciteturn11search4 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: yesterday; Thumamah Camp ... The above hotel prices are based on Trip.com for September 13-September 19.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nالسواحة: المملكة تُواصل بناء نموذج متكامل لجذب شركات الذكاء الاصطناعي وتعظيم الاستفادة منه ...السعودية (https://arabic.pressbee.net/amp/show10978982.html)\nciteturn11search5 [wordlim: 200] Published: 3 days ago; Crawled: 2 days ago; وبيّن السواحة أن المملكة تعمل بالشراكة مع القطاع الخاص على تطوير أكثر من 14 جيجاواط من القدرات الحوسبية، بما يدعم احتياجات شركات الذكاء الاصطناعي المتقدمة، ويخفض تكاليف التشغيل، ويرفع كفاءة البنية التحتية.وأبرز السواحة توسع المملكة في تطبيقات الذكاء الاصطناعي التوليدي والوكيلي والواقعي، من التطبيقات الصحية، إلى تمكين الموظفين الحكوميين بالوكلاء الأذكياء، وصولًا إلى استخدام الأنظمة الذاتية في قطاعات النقل والخدمات اللوجستية.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSaudi Arabia — Ajel English (https://english.ajel.sa/saudi-arabia?page=15)\nciteturn11search6 [wordlim: 200] Published: 3 